frontend/node_modules
frontend/dist
# The Playwright e2e image installs its own pinned @playwright/test inside the
# container (tests/Dockerfile.playwright `npm install`). When a developer has
# run the suite locally, `tests/e2e/node_modules` holds a different
# @playwright/test, and `COPY tests/e2e/ /tests/tests/e2e/` ships it into the
# image next to the pinned one -- Node then resolves specs against the local
# copy while the runner uses the pinned copy, and every spec dies with
# "Playwright Test did not expect test() to be called here" / "No tests found".
# Same for `test-results/`: local failure artifacts have no business in a
# build context. Both are gitignored; mirror that here.
tests/e2e/node_modules
tests/e2e/test-results
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.git
